# Editor
.vscode

# The api keys, each encrypted with a password (api-key-store/), and the
# temp file the key file is written through
api-keys.json
api-keys.json.tmp

# The local settings of the two Sheets scripts' Node versions and of
# crypto-price-filler: the values each lays over the ones written in its
# code or in its committed config-example.json. Beside each, a
# config-example.json, which git keeps, shows the settings with those
# values. The top config.json is committed: it lists the services whose
# keys the project keeps, in the order of priority the programs use until
# the owner ranks them, and holds no key.
/crypto-price-fetchers/config.json
/fetch-from-any-exchange/config.json
/fetch-from-any-exchange/crypto-price-filler/config.json

# The owner's own files: those a tool reads from its input/ folder, and
# those it writes in its output/ folder, by kind (output/csv/). Git keeps
# each folder by its .gitkeep, an empty file, and nothing else in it: the
# first rule of an output/ folder ignores all it holds, at any depth; the
# second takes its folders back, so git looks inside them; and !.gitkeep
# keeps each .gitkeep.
/fetch-from-any-exchange/crypto-price-filler/input/*
/fetch-from-any-exchange/crypto-price-filler/output/**
!/fetch-from-any-exchange/crypto-price-filler/output/**/
/summ-csv/input/*
/summ-csv/output/**
!/summ-csv/output/**/
!.gitkeep

# The Sheets file as `npm run build apps-script` writes it when there is
# no clipboard: it holds the api keys in the clear
/dist/

